  "response": "# Perspective Audit\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 Confirm escalated perspectives\n\nEscalated for deep review:\n- **Auditory Access** (HIGH)\n- **Screen Reader & Semantic Structure** (MEDIUM)\n\nPerspectives at LOW (not reviewed): Magnification & Reflow, Environmental Contrast, Vestibular & Motion Sensitivity, Keyboard & Motor Access, Cognitive & Neurodivergent.\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 Read reference files\n\nLoaded:\n1. `.claude/skills/perspective-audit/references/perspectives.md` \u2014 Sections for Auditory Access and Screen Reader & Semantic Structure only.\n2. `.claude/skills/perspective-audit/references/arrm-perspective-mapping.md` \u2014 Full mapping read.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 Read the artifact under review\n\nComponent analyzed: `VideoTutorialPage.jsx`. Key observations:\n- Custom `<video>` player with no native controls (`controls` attribute absent).\n- No `<track kind=\"captions\">` element present on the video.\n- Audio feedback (beeps) used for completion and error states without visual alternatives in markup.\n- Semantic structure includes `<main>`, headings, but lacks landmark labeling beyond `aria-label`.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 Run per-perspective checklists\n\n### Auditory Access Checklist Results\n\n| Item | Status | Evidence |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| Video with speech has `<track kind=\"captions\">` | **FINDING** | No `<track>` element in markup (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:26`) |\n| Audio elements have transcript/link | N/A | No standalone audio elements; video is primary media |\n| Media player controls keyboard-operable | PASS | All buttons/inputs are native HTML, Tab-reachable |\n| Visual indicators accompany auditory alerts | **FINDING** | Completion/error beeps lack visual counterparts in markup (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:42-53`) |\n| No audio auto-play without stop control | N/A | Video does not autoplay; user-initiated play only |\n\nRed flags triggered: None (no flashing, no missing media player controls).\n\n### Screen Reader & Semantic Structure Checklist Results\n\n| Item | Status | Evidence |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| Landmark regions present and correct | PASS | `<main>` used appropriately (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:70`) |\n| Heading hierarchy logical | PASS | Single `<h1>`, followed by `<h2>` in meta section (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:71, 96`) |\n| Informative images have alt; decorative `alt=\"\"` | N/A | No static images present |\n| DOM order matches visual reading order | PASS | Linear JSX structure follows expected flow |\n| Unique descriptive `<title>` | **FINDING** | No document title set in component (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx`) \u2014 depends on parent app, but not guaranteed here |\n| Link text describes purpose/context | N/A | No anchor links present |\n| `lang` attribute on `<html>` | **FINDING** | Not managed within this component; assumed inherited from app shell |\n| Foreign-language phrases wrapped in `lang` | N/A | None detected |\n| Form inputs have visible labels with association | PASS | Range sliders use `aria-label`; buttons have text content + aria-labels (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:78-90`) |\n| Error messages identify field and associate via `aria-describedby` | **FINDING** | No error message element or `aria-describedby` linkage for video errors (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:53`) |\n| Custom widgets use correct ARIA roles per APG | PASS | Controls follow standard patterns; no custom widget roles introduced |\n| Status messages use `aria-live` appropriately | **FINDING** | Time display uses `aria-live=\"off\"` \u2014 completion/error states not announced (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:84`) |\n\nRed flags triggered: None (landmarks present, form inputs labeled).\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 Format each finding\n\n---\n\n### Finding 1: Missing Captions Track on Speech Video\n**WCAG:** 1.2.2 Captions (Prerecorded)  \n**Perspective:** Auditory Access  \n**Severity:** CRITICAL  \n**Route to:** Content Author (secondary: Front-End Dev)  \n**Evidence:** `<video>` element at `VideoTutorialPage.jsx:26` contains no `<track kind=\"captions\">` child. Expected behavior states video has speech content throughout.  \n**Fix:** Add a `<track kind=\"captions\" src=\"[transcript-url]\" srclang=\"en\" label=\"English\">` element inside the `<video>` tag. Source must point to a valid VTT file with accurate, synchronized captions.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 2: Auditory Alerts Lack Visual Counterparts\n**WCAG:** 1.4.2 Audio Control  \n**Perspective:** Auditory Access  \n**Severity:** MAJOR  \n**Route to:** UX Design (secondary: Front-End Dev)  \n**Evidence:** Completion beep (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:42`) and error tone (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:50`) are triggered via `AudioContext` oscillators but have no corresponding visual indicators in the DOM. Users who cannot perceive audio will miss these state changes entirely.  \n**Fix:** Add visible UI feedback (e.g., toast notification, icon change, or status message) for both completion and error states. Ensure these elements are also announced to screen readers via `aria-live`.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 3: No Document Title Set in Component Scope\n**WCAG:** 2.4.2 Page Titled  \n**Perspective:** Screen Reader & Semantic Structure  \n**Severity:** MINOR  \n**Route to:** Front-End Dev (secondary: Content Author)  \n**Evidence:** `VideoTutorialPage.jsx` renders `<main>` and headings but does not set or manage a unique document title via `useEffect(() => { document.title = ... })`. Relies on parent app shell for titling.  \n**Fix:** Add dynamic title management within the component using React's `useEffect`:\n```jsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  document.title = `${title} - Video Tutorial`;\n}, [title]);\n```\n\n---\n\n### Finding 4: Error State Not Programmatically Associated with User\n**WCAG:** 3.3.1 Error Identification  \n**Perspective:** Screen Reader & Semantic Structure  \n**Severity:** MAJOR  \n**Route to:** Front-End Dev (secondary: UX Design)  \n**Evidence:** When `hasError` becomes true (`VideoTutorialPage.jsx:53`), no visible error message is rendered, and there is no element with an ID referenced by `aria-describedby` on the video or player container. Screen reader users receive no indication of failure.  \n**Fix:** Render a visually hidden but screen-reader-accessible error message when `hasError === true`, and associate it programmatically:\n```jsx\n{hasError && (\n  <div id=\"video-error-msg\" className=\"sr-only\">\n    Sorry, there was a problem loading the video. Please try again later.\n  </div>\n)}\n// On video element or wrapper:\naria-describedby={hasError ? \"video-error-msg\" : undefined}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Finding 5: Time Display Uses aria-live=\"off\", Suppressing Live Region Announcements\n**WCAG:** 4.1.3 Status Messages  \n**Perspective:** Screen Reader & Semantic Structure  \n**Severity:** MINOR  \n**Route to:** Front-End Dev (secondary: UX Design)  \n**Evidence:** The time display span at `VideoTutorialPage.jsx:84` uses `aria-live=\"off\"`, preventing screen readers from announcing updates. While not critical for playback, this suppresses potentially useful contextual information during seeking or scrubbing.  \n**Fix:** Change to `aria-live=\"polite\"` if real-time time announcements are desired, or leave as-is if deemed non-essential (acceptable trade-off depending on UX intent).\n\n---\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 Compile the summary\n\n## Perspective Audit Summary\n\n**Component/artifact reviewed:** VideoTutorialPage.jsx  \n**Perspectives escalated for deep review:** Auditory Access (HIGH), Screen Reader & Semantic Structure (MEDIUM)  \n**Perspectives at LOW (not reviewed):** Magnification & Reflow, Environmental Contrast, Vestibular & Motion Sensitivity, Keyboard & Motor Access, Cognitive & Neurodivergent\n\n### Findings by Severity\n\n| Severity | Count |\n|---|---|\n| CRITICAL | 1 |\n| MAJOR | 2 |\n| MINOR | 2 |\n| ENHANCEMENT | 0 |\n\n### Perspectives That Passed\n\nNone fully passed \u2014 all escalated perspectives had at least one finding.\n\n### Perspectives With Findings \u2014 Grouped by ARRM Role\n\n**Content Author**\n- Missing Captions Track on Speech Video \u2014 Auditory Access \u2014 CRITICAL \u2014 WCAG 1.2.2  \n*(Secondary: Front-End Dev)*\n\n**UX Design**\n- Auditory Alerts Lack Visual Counterparts \u2014 Auditory Access \u2014 MAJOR \u2014 WCAG 1.4.2  \n*(Secondary: Front-End Dev)*  \n- Error State Not Programmatically Associated with User \u2014 Screen Reader & Semantic Structure \u2014 MAJOR \u2014 WCAG 3.3.1  \n*(Secondary: UX Design)*\n\n**Front-End Dev**\n- No Document Title Set in Component Scope \u2014 Screen Reader & Semantic Structure \u2014 MINOR \u2014 WCAG 2.4.2  \n*(Secondary: Content Author)*  \n- Time Display Uses aria-live=\"off\", Suppressing Live Region Announcements \u2014 Screen Reader & Semantic Structure \u2014 MINOR \u2014 WCAG 4.1.3\n\n### Open Questions Requiring Human Verification\n\nNone identified in this audit pass. All findings are code-level and enforceable from source review. Caption accuracy, transcript completeness, and audio description coverage would require content author verification once infrastructure is added.\n\n### Recommended Next Step\n\n**REVISE** \u2014 One CRITICAL finding (missing captions) must be resolved before shipping. Two MAJOR findings should also be addressed to ensure full accessibility compliance across both escalated perspectives.",
